  "prefLabel": "Odb 204.02 Hearings",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Odb 204.02 Hearings. A non-adjudicative public hearing shall be held:\n\n(a) To receive evidence and testimony on reimbursement determinations and other matters required by the statute or rules;\n\n(b) For any matter for which the board is required by law or by these rules to hold a hearing that is not a contested case; and\n\n(c) For any matter for which the law does not require the board to hold a hearing but for which the board believes a public hearing would be of benefit.\n\nSource. #8490-B, eff 11-22-05; ss by #10481, eff 12-3-13; ss by #12941, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/odb100-600.html"
